+# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+# Today v2 ("Instrument") — layout, header and mode lamps.
+# Source of truth: design/v2/HANDOVER.md §3 (order), D10, D13, D14, §2.5.
+# Mockups: design/v2/mockups/a2.png (dark), a2-light.png (light).
+# Behind the ?ui=v2 flag (remembered in localStorage.ui_v2) until the default flips.
+# v1 (Dashboard) is untouched and keeps its own specs.
+# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+Feature: Today v2 layout — header, mode lamps and element order
+
+  Background:
+    Given the v2 UI is on (opened with ?ui=v2)
+
+  # ── Order (§3) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
+
+  Scenario: Today reads top to bottom in the designed order
+    When I open Today
+    Then I see, in order: the header, the mode lamps, the cut-load tape (when shown),
+      the gauge, the caution strip (when shown), TARGET · EATEN, the macro tapes,
+      LOG FOOD | QUICK ADD, the meal list, water, weight | est. TDEE, measurements,
+      workout, last 7 days
+    And there is no AI coach card
+
+  # ── Header (§3.1, D13) ───────────────────────────────────────
+
+  Scenario: The header shows the wordmark and a date line with the streak as text
+    When I open Today
+    Then the header reads "FUEL/LOG" with the slash in amber
+    And under it a date line like "FRI 20 NOV · DAY 3 STREAK"
+    And the streak is plain text in the date line, with no flame chip
+    And the uppercase is set by CSS, not typed into the text
+
+  Scenario: No streak yet
+    Given nothing has been logged today
+    Then the date line shows only the date
+
+  Scenario: The header stays visible while scrolling
+    When I scroll down Today
+    Then the header stays pinned at the top
+
+  Scenario: Offline and sync status live in the date line
+    Given the device is offline
+    Then the date line ends with "OFFLINE" in amber
+    When a sync message is showing
+    Then it appears in the date line, quietly, after the date
+
+  Scenario Outline: Header buttons open their screens
+    When I tap the "<button>" header button
+    Then the "<screen>" screen opens
+    Examples:
+      | button   | screen        |
+      | History  | history       |
+      | Badges   | achievements  |
+      | Settings | profile       |
+
+  Scenario: A new badge shows on the Badges button
+    Given a badge has just been earned
+    Then the Badges button carries an amber count bubble
+    And there is no glow
+
+  Scenario: The account chip appears only when signed in
+    Given I am signed in with Google
+    Then the header ends with a round avatar chip showing my Google photo
+    And when the photo is missing or fails, it shows my initial instead
+    When I tap the chip
+    Then Account opens
+    Given I am signed out
+    Then there is no avatar chip
+
+  # ── Mode lamps (§3.2, D10, D14) ──────────────────────────────
+
+  Scenario: One lamp is lit for the current mode
+    Given my mode is Cut
+    Then the CUT lamp is lit (amber tint, amber outline) and MAINTAIN and BULK are dark
+
+  Scenario: No lamp is lit while a custom target is set
+    Given I have set my own daily target
+    Then none of CUT, MAINTAIN or BULK is lit
+
+  Scenario: A diet break is Maintain, not a fourth lamp
+    Given I am on a diet break
+    Then MAINTAIN is lit
+    And there is no BREAK lamp and no BREAK label
+
+  Scenario Outline: Tapping a lamp asks for the mode through the one guarded path
+    When I tap the "<lamp>" lamp
+    Then requestMode("<mode>", "today") is called
+    And the lamp never writes the mode directly
+    Examples:
+      | lamp     | mode     |
+      | CUT      | cut      |
+      | MAINTAIN | maintain |
+      | BULK     | bulk     |
diff --git a/features/app-shell/06-mode-guard.feature b/features/app-shell/06-mode-guard.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..2c89abf
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/app-shell/06-mode-guard.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,62 @@
+# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+# One guarded mode path — design/v2/HANDOVER.md §7.5, §7.6, D10, D16.
+# Ruling: design/v2/reviews/early-return-ruling.md.
+# v2 only for now: v1's Dashboard keeps its own local guard (features/energy-safety/03).
+# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+Feature: Every mode change goes through requestMode
+
+  Background:
+    Given the v2 UI is on
+
+  Scenario: Every surface that changes mode uses requestMode(mode, source)
+    Then the Today lamps, Settings › Body & goal, committing a custom target and the
+      break-due sheet all call requestMode
+    And nothing else writes the mode
+    # TODO (Phase 0): a static test, in the styles.test.js pattern, that fails if any code
+    # calls handleSetMode/saveMode outside requestMode. Custom target (bug B4) still bypasses it.
+
+  Scenario: Maintain and Bulk are never guarded
+    Given I am mid-break with load remaining
+    When I request Maintain or Bulk
+    Then the mode changes at once with no confirm
+
+  Scenario: A short casual cut never sees the guard
+    Given my break began with load below the soft-nudge threshold
+    When I request Cut
+    Then the mode changes at once with no confirm
+
+  Scenario: Going back to Cut early asks once
+    Given I am mid-break and the break began at or above the soft-nudge threshold
+    When I request Cut from any surface
+    Then a bottom sheet asks "Back to cutting already?"
+    And the mode is not changed until I answer
+
+  Scenario: The confirm states the cost honestly, as an estimate
+    Given the confirm sheet is showing
+    Then it says "About {d} more rest days would finish this break"
+    And, when the remaining load is below the soft threshold, continues
+      "and if you cut now the next break reminder is likely in about {w} weeks at your cut target."
+    And, when the remaining load is at or above the soft threshold, continues
+      "and if you cut now the break reminder will be back in a few days."
+    And it always shows the factual line "This block began on {date}."
+    # {w} is computed at render from the remaining load at the CUT target's deficit
+    # ((soft − load) / dayCutLoad(cutTarget, maintenance)), never today's maintenance target
+    # (which would be infinite). It is whole weeks, "about", and never stored or shown again.
+
+  Scenario: Keep resting is the primary answer
+    When I tap "Keep resting"
+    Then the sheet closes and my mode stays Maintain
+
+  Scenario: Cut anyway is respected immediately
+    When I tap "Cut anyway"
+    Then my mode becomes Cut at once
+    And there is no second confirm, no cooldown and no "why?" form
+    And the tape resumes at its true level, amber at once if at or above the nudge
+    And no forecast or percentage recharged is shown afterwards
+    # Known bug B1 (out of scope for the UI slice): startDietBreak clears both snoozes,
+    # so after "Cut anyway" the nudge can reappear at once. Fix on main: Cut anyway sets
+    # nudgeAt = snoozeAt = now.
+
+  Scenario: Tapping the dimmed screen behind the sheet keeps resting
+    When I tap outside the sheet
+    Then it behaves as "Keep resting"
diff --git a/features/energy-safety/03-diet-break-intervention.feature b/features/energy-safety/03-diet-break-intervention.feature
index 840b5ff..2054374 100644
--- a/features/energy-safety/03-diet-break-intervention.feature
+++ b/features/energy-safety/03-diet-break-intervention.feature
@@ -394,3 +394,139 @@ Feature: A break is time not cutting — measured, encouraged, and guarded
     When I sign in on a different device
     Then that device shows the same remaining load and keeps draining from it
     And the guard behaves the same as it would have on my phone
+
+# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+# v2 UI ADDITIONS (2026-11) — design/v2/HANDOVER.md §7, D14–D16.
+# Applies only behind ?ui=v2. Every v1 scenario above still governs v1 and the logic.
+# Mockups: design/v2/mockups/a2-break.png, a2-break2.png.
+#
+# DISPLAY ONLY, LOGIC UNCHANGED: banking at 90 % of maintenance (D15) changes the DRAIN —
+# only banked days should pay down the load. That logic is NOT built yet: the drain still
+# counts every non-cut day as above. Until it is, v2 computes banked / under / unlogged per
+# day from history for display only, so the tape's "N OF 14 DAYS BANKED" can run behind
+# the fill (which still drains on every rest day). Spec 02 must record, when the logic
+# lands, that the food log is read ONLY to grant break credit.
+# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+
+Feature: Diet break — v2 cut-load tape, banking and sheets
+
+  Background:
+    Given the v2 UI is on
+
+  # ── The tape (§7.1) ────────────────────────────────────────
+
+  Scenario: The tape sits under the lamps as an instrument
+    When the tape is shown
+    Then it is labelled "CUT LOAD" on the left with the status on the right
+    And it has ticks over 0–84, a taller mark at the lean-adjusted nudge point and at the end
+    And it is captioned "0 · NUDGE · BREAK"
+    And the load number itself is never shown
+
+  Scenario: Hidden when there is nothing to show
+    Given I am cutting with less than CUT_BAR_MIN_LOAD of load, or I have no open block
+    Then there is no tape
+
+  Scenario: Cutting, below the nudge
+    Given I am cutting with load between CUT_BAR_MIN_LOAD and the nudge
+    Then the fill is neutral grey
+    And the right label is "{n} WEEKS", real weeks since the block began (rest days included)
+    And tapping the tape does nothing
+
+  Scenario: Cutting, at or above the nudge
+    Given I am cutting with load at or above the nudge
+    Then the fill and label are amber
+    When I tap the tape
+    Then the soft decision sheet opens: "Start a 2-week break" / "Not yet"
+    And "Not yet" hides the nudge for 7 days (onCutNudgeDismiss)
+
+  Scenario: Break due
+    Given my load is full (the hard threshold)
+    Then the right label reads "BREAK DUE · {n} WEEKS" in amber
+    When I tap the tape
+    Then a bottom sheet opens over a dimmed screen with the eyebrow "CUT LOAD FULL · {n} WEEKS IN A DEFICIT"
+    And the headline "Time for a diet break"
+    And "{n} weeks is a long stretch in a deficit. Let's spend a couple of weeks at maintenance."
+    And the primary button "Start a 2-week break" sets Maintain in one tap (onStartDietBreak)
+    And the secondary button "Remind me in 3 days" snoozes it (onCutPromptSnooze)
+    And there is no close and no "never ask again"
+    And the footnote reads "Your target moves to maintenance, about {M} kcal."
+
+  # ── On a break (§7.1–7.3) ──────────────────────────────────
+
+  Scenario: The tape drains in teal while on a break
+    Given I am in Maintain (or Bulk) with load remaining
+    Then MAINTAIN is lit and the tape fill is teal
+    And the right label reads "ON A BREAK · {banked} OF 14 DAYS BANKED"
+    And what has already drained shows as a dashed outline
+
+  Scenario Outline: Each finished break day is judged against 90 % of maintenance
+    Given yesterday was a break day with <intake>
+    Then it is <state>
+    Examples:
+      | intake                        | state                                         |
+      | at least 0.9 × maintenance    | banked (solid)                                |
+      | logged but under 0.9 × M      | a hatched gap, labelled "Not banked, under maintenance" |
+      | nothing logged                | a dashed pending gap, labelled "Not banked yet, not logged" |
+
+  Scenario: Hatched gaps turn amber at two or more
+    Given one break day was under
+    Then its gap is neutral grey
+    Given two or more break days were under
+    Then the gaps are amber
+
+  Scenario: Today is always in progress
+    Then the line "Today {eaten} of {0.9 × M} to bank it" sits under the tape
+
+  Scenario Outline: One status line, by priority W5 > W4 > W6 > W10
+    Given <situation>
+    Then the status line reads "<line>"
+    And "Today … to bank it" sits beneath it
+    Examples:
+      | situation                              | line                                                                   |
+      | two or more break days were under      | You're not taking an effective break. Eat at maintenance.             |
+      | yesterday was under                    | Yesterday was under maintenance, so it didn't count towards your break. |
+      | yesterday wasn't logged                | Yesterday wasn't logged. Log it                                        |
+      | the last 3 break days were all banked  | 3 for 3. This is what a break looks like.                              |
+
+  Scenario: "Log it" opens History to fill in yesterday
+    Given the status line reads "Yesterday wasn't logged."
+    When I tap "Log it"
+    Then the History screen opens
+
+  Scenario: Tapping the break tape explains it
+    When I tap the tape on a break
+    Then it shows "About {d} days to fully recharged." and "Recharging now sets up your next block."
+
+  # ── Going back to Cut early (§7.5) — see app-shell/06 ───────
+
+  Scenario: The early-return confirm uses the agreed copy
+    Given I am mid-break and the break began at or above the soft threshold
+    When I tap the CUT lamp
+    Then the sheet reads "Back to cutting already?"
+    And "About {d} more rest days would finish this break, …" with the forecast
+    And "This block began on {date}."
+    And offers "Keep resting" (primary) and "Cut anyway"
+
+  # ── Caution strip (O1 proposal, not yet approved) ──────────
+
+  Scenario: Only the most important caution shows, with a count of the rest
+    Given more than one caution applies today
+    Then one strip under the gauge shows the highest-priority caution
+    And a "+{n} more" control expands the others in place
+    # Priority: aggressive-cut acknowledgement (needs an answer) > low on fuel >
+    # weight up while cutting > held at minimum maintenance > eased to a steady pace >
+    # other target warnings > recharged.
+
+  Scenario: The aggressive-cut acknowledgement stays actionable
+    Given my own target is more than 1,000 kcal under maintenance and I have not acknowledged it
+    Then the strip shows "Not recommended" with "Yes, I understand"
+    When I tap it
+    Then onAckAggressiveCut is called
+
+  Scenario: Recharged can be dismissed from the strip
+    Given the block has just fully drained
+    Then the strip can show "Recharged" with a dismiss control (onDismissRecharged)
+
+  Scenario: The safe-minimum notice is gone (D6)
+    Given the safe minimum is applied
+    Then no notice says so; the floor itself still applies
